        " «يُغَسَّلُ وَ يُكَفَّنُ وَ يُصَلَّى عَلَيْهِ وَ يُدْفَنُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.441 - Ali ibn Ja'far asked his brother Imam Musa ibn Jafar Al-Kadhim (as) about a man who has been devoured by a wild animal or birds, leaving only his bones without flesh. He asked what should be done in such a case.\nImam (as) replied: \"He should be washed, shrouded, funeral prayers should be offered for him, and he should be buried”."
        ]
      }
